                <pb facs="0485" n="433" xml:id="pg433"/>


                <head><hi rendition="#bold">Memorandum From the Director of the United States
                        Information Agency (Shakespeare) to the President’s Assistant for National
                        Security Affairs (Kissinger)</hi><anchor n="5" xml:id="d168-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1972-03-23">March 23, 1972</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The attached internal memorandum, from me to the head of our Policy and Plans
                    office, was sharply criticized by Senator Fulbright during this morning’s USIA
                    Authorization Hearings before the Senate Foreign Relations Committee. Fulbright
                    took the position that its intent was to stir up trouble in a foreign
                    country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_SFJ_1">Frank Shakespeare<anchor n="6" xml:id="d168-f2"
                        /></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
